    "result_text": "The build is green. The full suite ran to `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema with an enum of the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), which generates the `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` type.\n\n2. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper that derives the segment:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevel.of(...) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the locality (via `CityRegion.localityOfCustomerCode`) is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL` (when locality is `UNKNOWN`).\n   - Returns the generated `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`, matching the existing pattern used by `AgeBand`/`ContactPreference`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a household-aware `ownerSegment(owner)` helper (it needs the `OwnerRepository` like `membershipLevel`) and a `@Mapping` targeting `ownerSegment`.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSegmentForKnownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
